1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,613
Picture a Mezo borrower at a safe ratio.

2
00:00:03,613 --> 00:00:08,998
A redemption takes their BTC anyway, sold at one dollar per MUSD,

3
00:00:08,998 --> 00:00:12,063
because their loan was first in line.

4
00:00:12,063 --> 00:00:16,288
On Mezo mainnet, redemptions hit loans 1,310 times.

5
00:00:16,288 --> 00:00:17,696
Liquidations, 28.

6
00:00:18,596 --> 00:00:21,504
Frontline is a redemption market for MUSD.

7
00:00:21,504 --> 00:00:26,282
Borrowers pay a small premium, and BTC holders called absorbers stand

8
00:00:26,282 --> 00:00:27,251
first in line.

9
00:00:28,151 --> 00:00:32,173
This is Mezo’s redemption line, read live from the chain.

10
00:00:32,173 --> 00:00:34,642
Pick a size and see where it stops.

11
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:38,811
I lock 0.2 BTC and borrow 6,000 MUSD.

12
00:00:38,811 --> 00:00:44,288
Before I sign, I see the absorber debt in front of me, and the

13
00:00:44,288 --> 00:00:44,994
premium:

14
00:00:44,994 --> 00:00:46,319
half a percent.

15
00:00:47,219 --> 00:00:54,547
Someone redeems 5,000 MUSD, here on a local fork of Mezo testnet with

16
00:00:54,547 --> 00:00:56,565
the real contracts.

17
00:00:56,565 --> 00:01:01,451
The absorber loan drops from 30,145 to 25,145.

18
00:01:01,451 --> 00:01:03,787
My loan does not move.

19
00:01:04,687 --> 00:01:06,775
Absorbers earn the premium.

20
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:11,879
A redemption swaps part of their BTC for MUSD at the oracle price,

21
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:13,735
with no loss in dollars.

22
00:01:14,635 --> 00:01:16,903
Frontline does not change MUSD.

23
00:01:16,903 --> 00:01:21,804
Our contracts own real troves and keep absorber loans at the front.

24
00:01:21,804 --> 00:01:25,682
Thirty-six tests run against the real MUSD contracts;

25
00:01:25,682 --> 00:01:29,412
a self-review fixed one high and two medium issues.

26
00:01:29,412 --> 00:01:31,315
Wallets use Mezo Passport.

27
00:01:32,215 --> 00:01:32,598
Next:

28
00:01:32,598 --> 00:01:36,820
outside users on testnet, then a capped mainnet launch.

29
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:41,580
So redemptions take BTC only from those who chose to be first.

